{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/260701-does-in-my-pocket-allow-you-to-pull-anything-out-of-anything","id":260701,"title":"Does \"In My Pocket\" Allow you to pull anything out of anything?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-19T09:46:16-07:00","id":260701,"title":"Does \"In My Pocket\" Allow you to pull anything out of anything?","content":"Does the &quot;In My Pocket&quot; embed allow you to pull anything out of anything? For example, pull a Flamethrower out of a trash can? I would think &quot;no&quot; since embeds are supposed to be subtle. I would think this would be more like a custom exploit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T13:31:20-07:00","id":260935,"title":"","content":"Anything that could fit in and be explained somehow as being there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T17:20:05-07:00","id":261056,"title":"","content":"Anything that would fit in the container, could reasonably be in the container, and not obviously established as not being in the container before hand. So, using &quot;In My Pocket&quot; will almost never let you produce a flame thrower, unless you happen to be digging up oil drums buried in the yard of a survivalist nut. He may have only buried rifles, but he's not here, and until you open the drum you don't know he DIDN'T bury a flamethrower or LAW rocket launcher...<br /> <br /> But no, mostly you won't be able to pull out things on that level, that falls into the purview of the &quot;Deep Pockets&quot; exploit.<br /> <br /> However, you could pull a .22 caliber derringer out of damn near anything, as long as you haven't had to go through a metal detector or full body search...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T13:59:35-07:00","id":263075,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your comments, but here's my concerns about allowing anything other than the last (above this one interpretation). So this means that other than the cap on damage, there's really no practical limit for what you can get, as long as there is some sort of accessible container near you. You could pull out a small nuclear device, a computer that has already been setup so that it is hacked into a command and control infrastructure, a gun that shoots bullets that do aggravated damage to Angels, etc. Yes, there's a Primium cap on damage (which is obviated by an Exceptional Success) and after 5 times you have to roll for Compromise with a bonus, but those are pretty trivial.<br /> <br /> Why are all the other embeds so subtle and modest while this one is anything-goes? You can duplicate the effect of nearly any other embed with this. Need to convince someone, voila, you pull out the incriminating photos you need. Need to get into the building? Volia, you have the exact paperwork, credentials, etc. You only really need this embed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T14:18:02-07:00","id":263107,"title":"","content":"No, you cannot pull out anything of that sort.<br /> <br /> You cannot pull out &quot;incriminating photo of the subject.&quot; If you had Deep Pockets and that incriminating photo elsewhere, you could. If you use In My Pocket and you want an &quot;incriminating photograph&quot; that's probably too particular a thing, you will get some kind of photo.<br /> <br /> In My Pocket doesn't do specific, pre-existing objects. That's Deep Pockets. It can give you general things.<br /> <br /> Are you trying to get into the locked room? In My Pocket means you have a lockpick, not necessarily the key.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 09-22-2014, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T15:43:04-07:00","id":263170,"title":"","content":"My thinking along these lines is just as every entry in Embeds Dramatic Failure section doesn't say &quot;dramatic failures by the way have to be dramatic,&quot; each embed isn't prefixed with &quot;embeds are subtle hacks of reality that don't draw the attention of the god machine because they are subtle.&quot; If they didn't have to be subtle and modest, the system wouldn't need exploits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T16:12:26-07:00","id":263206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PencilBoy99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/260701-does-in-my-pocket-allow-you-to-pull-anything-out-of-anything?p=263170#post263170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thinking along these lines is just as every entry in Embeds Dramatic Failure section doesn't say &quot;dramatic failures by the way have to be dramatic,&quot; each embed isn't prefixed with &quot;embeds are subtle hacks of reality that don't draw the attention of the god machine because they are subtle.&quot; If they didn't have to be subtle and modest, the system wouldn't need exploits.</div> </div> </div> </div>False criterion. There are Embeds that are <i>always a compromise to use</i>. The defining mechanical features of an Embed are as outlined in the Design Principles sidebar on page 124 of the corebook. The defining nature of an Embed is as stated in the section describing what Embeds are on the preceding page and in the lexicon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T16:24:41-07:00","id":263211,"title":"","content":"By RAW, In My Pocket doesn't have to be subtle. It just has to be possible and nonspecific. It's only subtle in the sense that none of the witnesses know for sure that the object wasn't there all along. The thing that makes Deep Pockets the Exploit version of the power is that a Demon could use it pull specific examples of the object out of their &quot;pocket&quot; even if someone knows the pocket is empty.<br /> <br /> So yes, in principle a Demon using In My Pocket could pull a flame thrower out of a trashcan with the embed, but they couldn't pull out their exploited Hellfire smg. They couldn't do either if someone in the scene saw the janitor empty the trash, unless they left the room long enough to make the state of the trashcan questionable again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T17:07:21-07:00","id":263269,"title":"","content":"So we're back again to my confusion. I'll accept that the text doesn't say that Embeds have to be subtle - I reread the section you pointed to and agree that it doesn't say that, except almost all of them seem subtle and modest. They give you a small bonus to an action, drop a door or two, allow you to add your roll successes to something. Not circumvent all obstacles.<br /> <br /> How is this exploit not game breaking and bizarrely way more powerful than almost any other embed. Why can't you pull out an exploited Hellfire smg? Why not an exploited gadget that heals all of your damage instantly? You can't pull out a specific one, but if there is possibly one in existence you can have one. Why not the key for a given lock? A mysterious gas that does very specific things? As long as it could exist, and hasn't been established as not being in the pocket, then he/she gets it.<br /> <br /> The only limiting phrase I see is &quot;he character can produce a badge or a form of identification, but it won\u2019t be tailored to the character and it won\u2019t stand up to any kind of inspection.&quot; But that doesn't say that he can't get a &quot;police badge.&quot; It's just that you can't pull out a badge that has your name on it, because that thing definitely doesn't exist (or you would have brought it with you lol). So why can't you pull out all of the financial records, or some incriminating photos for a person? Again, with this limitless power nearly any obstacle goes away. You'd be silly not to take it.<br /> <br /> Why take the embed that lets you soup up cars? Just open a garage door and volia, there's a car with all of your attributes?<br /> <br /> Also, why does it say &quot;that it works on things that are not literally pockets&quot; and list small things (&quot;insides of coats, purses, violin cases&quot;), but actually works on anything that can hold something? Does it work on a dumpster? Car? Warehouse? It doesn't say it doesn't.<br /> <br /> I think everybody above is &quot;right,&quot; its just that it ends up with either the embed is awesomely powerful in a way that doesn't seem to fit, or there's some text or understanding of it that is missing in the book.<br /> <br /> It doesn't say that you can just ask for &quot;the one thing my target want's most that can fit in my pocket?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":354,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","user":"PencilBoy99","date":". 09-22-2014, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T17:49:54-07:00","id":263279,"title":"","content":"I feel like you're not reading what's been said. You keep listing specific things when it's already been explained that specific things are not within the purview of the Embed.<br /> <br /> Yes it could in theory give you a gun. Yes it could in theory give you a badge. These are not specific things. Just flashing the badge might be enough for an informal or tense situation, while trying to use it to bluff your way into another situation, it won't stand up to scrutiny.<br /> <br /> So yes, you can get a police badge. The badge number probably isn't in the system, and while it'll work on some random joke Schmoe, if they call in to the police and ask about you, it'll reveal you were impersonating a police officer.<br /> <br /> Lastly, are we really saying the ability to pull out limited, non-specific items in certain circumstances are more powerful than any other Embed? Not only is that being unreasonable and silly, but how are you not considering what the competition is? In the company of Lucky Change, Shift Consequences, and Just Bruised, we're saying that In My Pocket is insanely powerful?<br /> <br /> That last bit is admittedly personal. Anyway. Let me. Repeat it once again, this Embed will not get you specific items, a Hellfire SMG is a gadget, and no gadget is generic, you cannot pull one of those out with this Embed. You need the Exploit for that. While I'm not entirely certain there's a limit on what you could use the power on, going by your garage example, you cannot get a car with your attributes or whatever, that's a specific item. You could, in this theory, probably get a car, but what that car will be is dictated by the same chance and circumstances that you found it with. Again, if you. Want to pull out the car, you need the Exploit. Randomly pulling objects out of your ass is actually NOT that useful in the scheme of things, when they're generic. It's pretty cool though.<br /> <br /> This is why the Exploit and the Embed are two separate powers. Because the Embed's scope and function are different. If you want to pull your arsenal out of nowhere, then you better do your prep and buy Deep Pockets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 09-22-2014, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T17:57:37-07:00","id":263281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PencilBoy99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/260701-does-in-my-pocket-allow-you-to-pull-anything-out-of-anything?p=263269#post263269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">limitless power</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be blunt, because indulging you clearly hasn't done any good:<br /> <br /> <i><b>You are blatantly ignoring what the power actually does and what people are telling you in the name of persisting in repeatedly broadcasting a delusional and exaggerated complaint. This is annoying and unlikely to result in future assistance being rendered. Please stop.</b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T18:01:28-07:00","id":263284,"title":"","content":"Apologies, I'll drop it. I think the quote that is being referenced is &quot;cannot produce an object belonging to or in the possession of another person (so the demon could produce a cell phone, but not a specific person\u2019s cell phone)&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":354,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","user":"PencilBoy99","date":". 09-22-2014, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T04:25:28-07:00","id":268162,"title":"","content":"PencilBoy99 actually pm'd me with this question: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PencilBoy99</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry to bother you but my group is struggling with the &quot;In my Pocket&quot; embed and was hoping you can provide a ruling. One player wants to use it to pull anything out of a container - for example, a military grade Flamethrower (which i'm guessing would have to do around +5 lethal minimum).<br /> <br /> Another interpretation of it is that this is game-breaking - there's essentially no limit on what you can do with it. Why have any other embed or ever use an exploit? Need to get into some place? You have the key, detailed blueprints to the building's secret interior, incriminating documents on the person you need to bribe, a cell phone that has already hacked into the Infrastructure's network, a gun with bullets that do aggravated damage to angels. Embeds are supposed to be subtle hacks to reality, that could be explained by mere chance. <br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>My reply, since he seems not to have seen it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a thread about this with some pretty good responses, but sure:<br /> <br /> In My Pocket lets you pull anything out of your pocket (or an appropriately-sized receptacle) that <i>hasn't been established not to be there</i>. As such, pulling something out of a pocket that wouldn't fit in said pocket doesn't work, because although we've never established that the elephant wasn't in my coat, it couldn't have fit in there to begin with. <br /> <br /> Likewise, one of the playtesters had a thing where a player pulled a celebrity's cell phone out, but that doesn't work unless the celebrity has not seen the phone in a while *and* the character actually had access to it. Same thing with the &quot;incriminating documents;&quot; pulling them out with In My Pocket presumes they exist, that the character had access to them, *and* that they're conclusively not anywhere else. <br /> <br /> It seems like you have a handle on how it's supposed to work, so run it that way. Also, while Embeds can be pretty potent, remember that any really reality-breaking (or stretching) use, especially repeated use, can cause compromise or get the God-Machine's attention. Don't let your players spam a power or game the system. Not only is the system not set up for that kind of play, it's counter to the intent of the game, and like a microwave, I can't guarantee things won't burst into flames if used in a manner other than intended. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>To address one of the things brought up in the thread: Could you pull a Gadget with Hellfire worked into it from your pocket using this Embed? Answer: Sure, provided that <i>the Gadget exists </i>(meaning you made it already or otherwise know that it exists), that <i>it could fit in your pocket</i> (duh), and <i>it hasn't been established that it's not there </i>(if your ring-mate said earlier in the mission, &quot;hey, Bingo, do you have that fire-make-thingie?&quot; and you say &quot;naw, lent it to my gramma for making creme brulee,&quot; then no, you can't pull it out because we know where it is - gramma making dessert. Make sure you cal her later).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T07:16:17-07:00","id":268248,"title":"","content":"Okay, so then the difference with the Exploit is that it doesn't matter what the size of the object is as long as you can lift it out of the receptacle, and it doesn't matter whether it's been established that you don't have the object?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T07:18:45-07:00","id":268251,"title":"","content":"Great clarifications. So (1) it needs to be pocket sized, (2) not in the receptacle, (3) something the Demon KNOWS exists and could have had access to, (4) something that hasn't been established not to be somewhere else. So not a: Flamethrower (since doesn't fit in a pocket sized receptacle), incriminating document's you've never seen, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3927-demon15","name":"Demon15","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T18:34:52-07:00","id":268681,"title":"","content":"More or less. If you could plausibly pull that object out of your pocket, you can do so.<br /> <br /> The example in the book about a metal-detector security screen is a really good one - If you've gone through a metal detector security scan (at say an airport or state function) then it's a plausible impossibility for the object in your pocket to be metallic. The security scan already established that you don't have a metal object in your pockets. So you couldn't pull out a metal object (such as a standard firearm or something) out of your pocket. You could perhaps pull out a ceramic knife, however :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}